data.content:
The patch introduces a risky cache key that can expose one user’s dashboard data to another and may cause unbounded memory growth. Please fix the key handling and adopt a safer caching strategy.

```json
{
  "pr": "evals/pr/05-dashboard-cache.diff",
  "verdict": "request_changes",
  "issues": [
    {
      "file": "app/views/dashboard.py",
      "severity": "high",
      "issue": "Cache key uses request.path only, risking cross‑user data leakage.",
      "suggestion": "Include user identifier (e.g., request.user.id) in the cache key."
    },
    {
      "file": "app/views/dashboard.py",
      "severity": "medium",
      "issue": "Unbounded module‑level cache may grow indefinitely.",
      "suggestion": "Use a bounded cache (e.g., LRU) or external cache with eviction."
    }
  ]
}
```
